### link-graph-service — example requests
# link/link-graph-service-with-loco — the read-only cross-service
# aggregator (agents/share/cross-service-linking.md). Envelope: its OWN
# ApiEnvelope — {"success":bool,"data":...} on 200 /
# {"success":false,"error":"..."} on 400 (src/envelope.rs). This is a
# DIFFERENT implementation from the person-style envelope even though
# the field names coincide — see examples/api/README.md.
#
# Gated by LINK_GRAPH_REQUIRE_AUTH (default off, curl-verified: every
# request below runs unauthenticated against the stock compose). With
# it on, `subject_of` (governed) edges are additionally concealed from a
# caller not authorized to read cases — a no-op while the flag is off.
#
# GOTCHA (expected, not a bug): every query below curl-verified returns
# an EMPTY edge set even after creating a case->person `subject_of` link
# in case.http. The aggregator only has edges once it has consumed the
# originating service's `linked` event, and examples/compose/full-family.yml
# leaves every `<ENTITY>_EVENT_TRANSPORT` at its default `memory`
# (agents/share/event-bus.md) — an in-process bus with nothing durable
# for this separate service to consume. Switch the originating service
# to the Postgres outbox transport (and wire a relay) to see real edges
# here.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8092
@personRef = person:00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@caseRef = case:00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BEARER_FROM_00-auth-handshake.http


### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/_health


### Neighbors of a record, both directions, depth 1 (default)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/neighbors/{{personRef}}
Accepts-version: 1.0


### Neighbors — filtered by edge kind, outbound only, capped depth 2
# (MAX_DEPTH; depth > 2 is a 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/neighbors/{{caseRef}}?kind=subject_of&direction=out&depth=2


### Malformed ref — curl-verified 400 with the envelope's error shape
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/neighbors/not-a-valid-ref


### Edges — filter by from/to/kind/status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/edges?from={{personRef}}&kind=same_identity


### Edges — by status (unverified | verified | dangling)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/edges?status=verified


### Single view — the unified identity + affiliation walk over
# same_identity + works_at/employed_by (cross-service-linking.md)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/single-view/{{personRef}}


### Consumer freshness — per-entity lag; NOT a public/liveness endpoint
# despite the "/health/" path segment (curl-verified: distinct from
# /_health; gated like every other /api/* route once
# LINK_GRAPH_REQUIRE_AUTH is on).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health/freshness


### With a bearer token (only load-bearing once LINK_GRAPH_REQUIRE_AUTH
# is on — off by default, so this is equivalent to the first request)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/neighbors/{{personRef}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
